  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "20344912-7285-44f2-88f8-3d3758c4b2eb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<strong>Now that we've confirmed our data has no NaN values and we understand the data distribution, we need to train our data using Logistic Regression to reach a final model that can be used to predict new patients (due to the question's requirement regarding the probability of having a heart attack and the presence of 0 and 1 values, we use this model).</strong>\n",
    "<p>How to do it:</p>\n",
    "<ul>\n",
    "    <p><input type='checkbox' checked> The first and most important step is to normalize the data using scaling.</p>\n",
    "    <p><input type='checkbox' checked> The second step is to split the data into training and test sets.</p>\n",
    "    <p><input type='checkbox' checked> The third step is to find the best parameters for the Logistic Regression model using GridSearchCV.</p>\n",
    "    <p><input type='checkbox' checked> The next step is to build the model with the selected parameters and review the results of the confusion matrix and classification report.</p>\n",
    "    <p><input type='checkbox' checked> The final step is to predict for a new patient, and to consider that if the prediction result is greater than 0.4 (or 40%), there is a risk of a heart attack.</p>\n",
    "</ul>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "91740030-a626-4b90-bdac-4cb707b7b1ae",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ss = StandardScaler()\n",
    "\n",
    "x = df.drop('output',axis=1)\n",
    "ss.fit(x)\n",
    "x = ss.transform(x)\n",
    "\n",
    "y= df['output']"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "1a0a6bc7-b130-49af-b900-ecda6e1c738c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "x_train, x_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(x, y, test_size=0.25, random_state=0)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "46a87e48-d79a-49b4-8c7f-e4449aaaaebb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Best parameters: {'C': 0.01, 'penalty': 'l2', 'solver': 'saga'}\n",
      "Best cross-validation accuracy: 0.83\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "lr = LogisticRegression()\n",
    "\n",
    "params_grid = {\n",
    "    'penalty': ['l1','l2'],\n",
    "    'C': [0.001, 0.01, 0.1, 1, 10, 100],\n",
    "    'solver': ['liblinear','saga']\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "grid_search = GridSearchCV(lr, params_grid, cv=5, scoring='accuracy')\n",
    "grid_search.fit(x_train, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Best parameters: {grid_search.best_params_}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Best cross-validation accuracy: {grid_search.best_score_:.2f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "00af4a43-c00a-42d6-87c4-09d8bf8d8440",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Accuracy of model = 0.83\n",
      "\n",
      "Confustion Matrix = \n",
      "[[22 11]\n",
      " [ 2 41]]\n",
      "\n",
      "Classification Report = \n",
      "              precision    recall  f1-score   support\n",
      "\n",
      "           0       0.92      0.67      0.77        33\n",
      "           1       0.79      0.95      0.86        43\n",
      "\n",
      "    accuracy                           0.83        76\n",
      "   macro avg       0.85      0.81      0.82        76\n",
      "weighted avg       0.84      0.83      0.82        76\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "model = LogisticRegression(C=0.01, penalty='l2', solver= 'saga')\n",
    "model.fit(x_train, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "target = model.predict(x_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "acc_score = accuracy_score(y_test,target)\n",
    "con_matrix = confusion_matrix(y_test,target)\n",
    "class_report = classification_report(y_test,target)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Accuracy of model = {acc_score:.2f}\\n\")\n",
    "print(f\"Confustion Matrix = \")\n",
    "print(con_matrix)\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Classification Report = \")\n",
    "print(class_report)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
